     5	    """ Out of list of strings, return the longest one. Return the first one in case of multiple
     6	    strings of the same length. Return None in case the input list is empty.
     7	    >>> longest([])
     8	
     9	    >>> longest(['a', 'b', 'c'])
    10	    'a'
    11	    >>> longest(['a', 'bb', 'ccc'])
    12	    'ccc'
    13	    """
